    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town began in 1823 as Mt. Salus, a frontier settlement that grew around a spring called Swafford's Spring.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clinton%2C_Mississippi"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Mississippi College, founded in 1826, is the state’s oldest college and the first Baptist university in the world to grant degrees to women.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        27,
